					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 4: MOVING BETWEEN POINTS\n\nIn this example we're taking the points from the Circle Pattern node and read them one by one using the Read node.\nWe use a unipolar Saw with an amplitude equal to the size of the pattern to cycle through all the indices.\nNote that the Read node is set to Linear interpolation, this way we get smooth movement between the points.\n\nThe Saw is also used to rotate the triangle shape in the Transform node.\nIn the end we render out the shape, add some Drop Shadow and create a feedback loop using a Video Mixer."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 742.988037109375,
					"width": 2330.70263671875,
					"x": 107.18662261962890625,
